div.p:
As steps directed toward the achievement of these common objectives, the four governments resolve:
1) to act to hasten the conclusion of a treaty of peace with Japan so that Japan may assume at an early date the responsibilities and obligations of a peaceful member of the Pacific community;
2) to consult together, with other nations of the Pacific area, and with members of the United Nations regarding measures which may be taken within the framework of the United Nations Charter to safeguard the freedom, independence, well being and security of the nations of the Pacific area.
